# `xs[i]!` answers an effect (book ch02, ch04), so reading a field of what it
# answers should be refused by `kanso check` the way `length os/args` is
# ("this is an effect ... open it with `.>`").
#
# should: error[effect] at check time, pointing at `s.first`.
# does:   no compile-time refusal; every engine stops at run time with
#         error[runtime]: `.` reads a field of a record, not <io>
#         Inside a module (re/classes.kso in this port) `kanso check` said
#         ok and `kanso test` printed the location as `re:60:24`, the
#         module directory rather than the file.
#
# run: kanso play bugs/strict_index_field_read.kso
type span
  first
  last

fn first_of spans
  s = spans[1]!
  s.first

print "{first_of [(span 1 2)]}"
